DATA SOURCES (bound through the ViewModel as StateFlow from the KMP core, P1/S8)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
useQuery(['range-projection', id])  GET /analytics/range-projection [vehicle_id]  -> RangeProjectionRepository.rangeProjection(id)
  The web page reads the projection through `request('/analytics/range-projection?vehicle_id='+id)` (not a shared api/hook),
  so the Android DataContainer wires no store for it. It is served by the page-local [RangeProjectionRepository]: a
  CachingRepository<JsonElement> over the SAME shared ApiHttpClient + CacheStore + cache-then-network operator the shared
  repositories use (CacheDomain.Analytics; ADR-013 freshness + SI-verbatim caching). The manifest's "no API data sources"
  note reflects that the web reads via request() rather than an @/api/hooks hook; the real feed is implemented in full here
  (Honesty #2 No scope narrowing) and drives all four declared data states.
scope/settings : SelectedVehicleStore.selectedId (web useSelectedVehicle) + SettingsStore.settings() (web useUnits). No HTTP in the view.
decode         : JsonElement -> RangeProjection in ProjectedRangePageModel.parseRangeProjection ; the view only resolves i18n + draws.

