=== SUMMARY ===
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data sources : 1 read bound as StateFlow via ProjectedRangePageViewModel -> projectedRangePageSourceOf():
               RangeProjectionRepository.rangeProjection (web useQuery '/analytics/range-projection') over the shared
               ApiHttpClient + CacheStore. Scope = SelectedVehicleStore (web useSelectedVehicle); units = SettingsStore.settings()
               (web useUnits). No HTTP in the view.
charts       : RadialGauge (web RadialGauge, A3 Compose-Canvas) + AreaChartWrapper (web AreaChart, A3 Vico wrapper) from the
               A3 components.charts library; the web <ReferenceLine x={battery_level}> becomes a ChartVerticalMarker rail
               (Vico 2.0 has no overlay reference line — same affordance as the BatteryHealthPage precedent). Compose-native,
               never a webview.
si/units     : SI read off the wire; rendered only at the display boundary via the shared UnitFormatter — scenario range
               km->display via distance(range_km*1000), scenario speed km/h->display via speed(speed_kmh/3.6), scenario
               temperature C->display via temperature(temp_c), capacity Wh->display via energy(usable_capacity_wh). The
               always-km estimate cards (your/tesla) and the projection-curve km values render verbatim, exactly as the web
               page does (web fmtNumber + ' km' / YAxis unit=' km' — web does not convert these). No miles/°F/psi stored/computed.
states       : range-projection is the gate (loading/empty/error/success). The what-if, matrix and scenario sections each
               render their own content-or-empty surface (noWhatIf / noMatrix / noScenarios), so no section is ever hidden
               (web per-section truthiness). Documented divergence (Honesty #9): a no-projection / no-vehicle payload routes to
               the friendly common.noData empty surface via the model hasData gate — a reasonable adaptation of the web page,
               which leaves the query disabled and renders per-section skeletons/empties when no vehicle is selected.
i18n         : every visible UI string resolves from res/values/strings.xml via stringResource (27 page keys + the generic
               chrome keys). Non-i18n literals (" km", "%", "Wh/km", "km/h", "°C", the matrix temp/speed bucket category
               labels, and the scenario "drives" count noun) are rendered verbatim exactly as the web source renders them —
               the web has no i18n key for any of these, so reproducing them literally is the faithful-parity choice
               (Honesty #9 No silent drift; ADR-014 unit-literals carve-out, matching the BatteryHealthPage precedent).
a11y/theme   : the projection-curve ChartContainer carries accessibleDescription (web aria); RadialGauge exposes a merged
               contentDescription; matrix speed-bucket headers carry a semantics contentDescription; icons decorative
               (contentDescription=null); all color via MaterialTheme.colorScheme + ChartPalette (TeslaTokens.chart) +
               TeslaTokens.status (A2 tokens) — dynamic color + dark theme; typography via the role components
               (PageTitle/SectionTitle/PanelTitle/BodyText/Caption/HelperText/MetricValue/MetricLabel). Compose-native (no webview).
